Launching a new business in Cardiff? Your first website has a different job from an established company's. It needs to make a new name look credible, explain what you do in a few seconds and start bringing in enquiries, all without eating the budget you need for everything else.

> "Your first website doesn't need to be perfect. It needs to be live, fast, and working for you."

If you're an established Cardiff business looking for a new or better website, see our main [web design Cardiff](/web-design-cardiff/) page instead.

## Three ways to launch

**1. No upfront cost: managed starter website from £20 a month inc. VAT**

The cheapest way to get a professional website live. Domain, hosting, updates and support are included, so there's nothing to set up or maintain yourself. It suits sole traders and new service businesses that want to keep cash in the business. See [managed starter websites for Cardiff](/managed-starter-websites-cardiff/).

**2. Own it outright: one-page WordPress website from £199**

A single page that covers who you are, what you offer, the areas you serve and how to contact you. You own the website, and it can grow into a multi-page site later without starting again.

**3. Not launched yet: a pre-launch page**

If your product or service isn't ready, a pre-launch page explains the idea and collects sign-ups from people who want to hear when you open. We built this kind of site for [Priva-Cy](/portfolio/priva-cy/), a Welsh privacy start-up, with a register-your-interest form so they could build a list before launch.

## What start-ups usually get wrong with a first website

- **Paying for pages they don't need yet.** Start with the pages that bring in enquiries and add more as you learn what customers ask for.
- **Building on something they can't move.** Locked website builders make it expensive to grow or leave. We build on WordPress, which you can take to any host.
- **Forgetting Google.** A new business has no reviews or history yet, so clear page titles, local wording and a Google Business Profile matter even more.
- **No clear next step.** Every page should make it obvious how to call, book or ask for a quote.

## What's included for Cardiff start-ups

- A mobile-first design that makes a new business look established
